## Course-level checks

Each year has a mid-year check and a year-end check. Each is the Check session of the unit it follows, widened: the unit's own unseen plan page and watched rehearsal (so the unit is checked there, not twice), plus one or two items sampled from the year's earlier units on new invented cases, in one 40-minute session; its Respond session is the unit's Respond session, reteaching the steps the sheet shows "not yet" across the unit and the sampled items. They sit after the third unit of each year (sessions 30 and 31, weeks 15 and 16) and after the sixth (sessions 63 and 64, week 32). Grades 9 to 12 have no after-core rule but the finals week (frame-write, "After-core courses"; CALENDAR.md stagger rules 3 and 4), so the year-end check sits in week 32, the finals week, and the mid-year check at the middle of the year; no week was moved to step around another after-core course's check (the lead's calendar pass, For the lead 10). Unit sheets are thrown away at the end of their unit (Evidence); a check's sheet is kept only until its respond session, then thrown away. Every unit is checked by its own end-of-unit assessment, and the units before each check are sampled again in it, so every unit of the year is sampled twice. Grade 12's year-end check is the band's last. On the short path each check and its respond share one session, the shared Check and Respond of the unit before it; where seniors leave early, grade 12's year-end check runs in unit 24's short-path form in the school's last senior week.

