### Library

AASL V.D.1 is taught with SM3 (units 1, 11 and 14, owned in unit 20), V.D.2 with SA8 (units 2, 12 and 14, owned in unit 20) and III.D.2 with RS4 (units 6, 11 and 16, owned in unit 21): no SEL unit waits on library. docs/courses/library/STANDARD.md section 4 and data/plans/library-excluded.csv place them in SEL. The grade 12 owner rows (g12-sm-stay-on-task, g12-sa-skills-grow, g12-rel-teamwork) and units 20 and 21 name them; they move into the rows' standard cells once scripts/progression.py accepts AASL ids for SEL (For the lead 3).

## For the lead

1. **Unit sizes.** q-fix-sel-1 followed exactly (four of 11, two of 10, 64 a year): each course-level check is the Check and Respond of the unit before it, which the 40-minute session holds, as the 3 to 5 frame did; unlike the K to 2 pilot's 11/8.
2. **Year-end check in week 32.** The finals week, after each year's last unit (frame-write, "Grades 6 to 12"); mid-year checks in weeks 15 and 16.
3. **AASL ids for SEL.** scripts/progression.py and scripts/frame.py reject AASL.V.D.1, V.D.2 and III.D.2 in sel.csv standard cells; validator support is needed before they move there.
4. **Health 9 to 12 side.** Health is one grade 9 fall semester; its SEL table should name SEL units 1, 2, 4, 6, 10 and 17, and its rows gain cross_subject leans to SEL.
5. **PE 9 to 12 side.** Its SEL row is still Pending; PE units 6 and 21 to 23 come after their SEL units and can open with SEL's plan pages.
6. **Spanish family notes.** 24 notes need a translation agent's read; no brief for that read exists.
7. **Supply ceiling.** None set for SEL; about $60 a year printing, $240 for the band, plus up to about $20 a pilot (Cory's money call).
8. **Computer science grades 11 and 12.** Frames not written; four SEL rows lean on them with no unit numbers (grades 9 and 10 cited).
9. **Grading or credit.** An advisory course with no grades in STANDARD; whether schools may give credit is a scope call for Cory.
10. **After-core calendar pass.** SEL checks were placed in weeks 15, 16 and 32 without dodging other after-core courses' checks, per the brief.
11. **SO6 cases.** Mendez (grade 9), Brown (10), Morgan (11) and Heart of Atlanta (12); the 3 to 5 and 6 to 8 frames should not reuse the later three.
12. **SEL 6 to 8 frame.** Written beside this one; Seams cites its grade 8 units 13 to 18 and card forms; its Handed on table and this Picked up table should be read together once.
13. **Sources.** No downloads or sign-ins were used; the court and museum pages under Base text were not read here and need the sensitivity agent's read (any that block go to "browser check").
14. **Grade 12 early leave.** Unit 24 folds to its short path where seniors finish before week 32; the school's last senior week is the check week.

