g9-soc-thankful | ~CASEL.Social Awareness.5 | in: | out: | cross: | Unit 4, Relationships that are good for me. The student designs a small gratitude habit for an invented student's school week (who to thank, how and when), names its trade-off (time, feeling awkward), and judges after the case week whether it changed how the people around responded. Step up from grade 8: from thanks for one costly help to a habit of thanks planned and checked.
g9-soc-fair-rules | ~CASEL.Social Awareness.6 | in: | out: | cross: | Unit 5, Norms, media and influence. The student applies the fairness questions to an invented school norm (seniors-only tables in the commons) and to a settled case the courts have ruled on, then designs a plan to change the school norm through school channels, with its trade-offs, and judges which part would work best. Step up from grade 8: from naming what a change cost to designing a change plan. Teacher note: settled facts the courts have ruled on, taught with dignity; current political disputes are not SEL content.
