g9-rds-ask-questions | ~CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.1 | in:stop-think-choose | out:stop-think-choose | cross:ela:e9-ri-argument-evaluate (judging whether reasoning holds and evidence is relevant) | Unit 5, Norms, media and influence. Before deciding on an invented school-wide issue (a new phone rule), the student plans the questions to ask, the sources to check and what would change their mind, then judges after the case whether the questions found what mattered. Step up from grade 8: from staying open under friends' pressure to planning an open inquiry.
g9-rds-check-facts | ~CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.2 | in:stop-think-choose | out:stop-think-choose | cross:math:alg1-data-displays (comparing distributions with plots before a choice) | Unit 5, Norms, media and influence. The student checks an invented claim spreading at school ("most students sleep six hours") against a class data set shown in two plots, plans a decision on what the data back, names what the data cannot show, and judges the decision with the look-back step. Step up from grade 8: from weighing evidence under time pressure to a data check designed and judged.
g9-rds-think-ahead | ~CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.4 | in:stop-think-choose | out:stop-think-choose | cross: | Unit 5, Norms, media and influence. The student lays out the short- and long-term results of options in an invented case (posting a clip of a class mishap that would get views), plans the choice with its trade-off, and later judges it against how the story unfolds. Step up from grade 8: from judging a costly choice afterward to planning ahead with a review built in.
g9-rds-careful-thinking | ~CASEL.Responsible Decision-Making.5 | in:stop-think-choose | out:stop-think-choose | cross: | Unit 5, Norms, media and influence. The student runs the six-step stop-think-choose on an invented choice pushed by a trending post, then compares it with the same choice made on a shortcut, and writes where careful thinking changed the result. Step up from grade 8: from thinking against a clock to judging a whole process against a shortcut.
