### Handed on to Social and Emotional Learning, Grades 9 to 12

Each grade 8 owner row hands on to the grade 9 row of its sub-skill, which assumes it. The grade 9 units below are those of the grades 9 to 12 frame (docs/courses/social-and-emotional-learning-grades-9-to-12/frame.md, "Picked up from Social and Emotional Learning, Grades 6 to 8"), whose table names these same grade 8 rows by their grade 8 unit (this frame's units 13 to 18).

| This course hands on | Unit here | Row that picks it up (grade 9 unit) | What grade 9 does with it |
|---|---|---|---|
| g8-rds-ask-questions (RD1) | 13 | g9-rds-ask-questions (unit 5) | From staying open under friends' pressure to planning an open inquiry. |
| g8-rds-check-facts (RD2) | 13 | g9-rds-check-facts (unit 5) | From weighing evidence under time pressure to a data check designed and judged. |
| g8-rds-think-ahead (RD4) | 13 | g9-rds-think-ahead (unit 5) | From judging a costly choice afterward to planning ahead with a review built in. |
| g8-rds-careful-thinking (RD5) | 13 | g9-rds-careful-thinking (unit 5) | From thinking against a clock to judging a whole process against a shortcut. |
| g8-sa-feel-think-link (SA5) | 13 | g9-sa-feel-think-link (unit 2) | From slowing one chain under pressure to planning where to break a loop that repeats. |
| g8-rds-who-is-affected (RD7) | 13 | g9-rds-who-is-affected (unit 5) | From weighing who is affected against popularity to a designed option checked for gaps. |
| g8-sa-tell-truth (SA4) | 14 | g9-sa-tell-truth (unit 3) | From choosing the true action at a price to planning how to carry it out. |
| g8-sa-who-i-am (SA1) | 14 | g9-sa-who-i-am (unit 3) | From holding values under group push to planning how identity grows. |
| g8-sa-my-strengths (SA2) | 14 | g9-sa-my-strengths (unit 3) | From using one strength at a cost to an asset plan across settings. |
| g8-sa-snap-judgments (SA6) | 14 | g9-sa-snap-judgments (unit 3) | From checking a judgment a group shares to a plan for testing one's own. |
| g8-rel-say-no (RS6) | 14 | g9-rel-say-no (unit 4) | From holding one costly no to a plan made before the pressure arrives. |
| g8-soc-read-situation (SO7) | 14 | g9-soc-read-situation (unit 1) | From reading rising stakes in one moment to planning across settings and judging the plan. |
| g8-sa-what-interests-me (SA9) | 14 | g9-sa-what-interests-me (unit 1) | From weighing one interest's worth to designing a small test of interests. |
| g8-sa-i-can-try (SA7) | 14 | g9-sa-i-can-try (unit 1) | Belief turned into a designed plan with its own test. |
| g8-sa-name-feelings (SA3) | 15 | g9-sa-name-feelings (unit 2) | From naming feelings as pressure builds to reading a pattern and planning for it. |
| g8-sa-skills-grow (SA8) | 15 | g9-sa-skills-grow (unit 2) | From choosing among ways to practice to designing and testing the whole plan. |
| g8-sm-big-feelings (SM1) | 15 | g9-sm-big-feelings (unit 2) | From choosing one response in a high-stakes moment to a plan made ahead. |
| g8-sm-calm-down (SM2) | 15 | g9-sm-calm-down (unit 2) | From a weekly plan chosen from the menu to a plan built and judged. |
| g8-sm-stay-on-task (SM3) | 15 | g9-sm-stay-on-task (unit 1) | The student builds the focus plan rather than choosing what to put off in one week. |
| g8-sm-plan-and-tidy (SM5) | 15 | g9-sm-plan-and-tidy (unit 1) | From cutting and moving clashing commitments to building and testing a whole system. |
| g8-soc-their-view (SO1) | 16 | g9-soc-their-view (unit 6) | From taking one costly view to planning how to test that one has it right. |
| g8-soc-care-when-struggle (SO3) | 16 | g9-soc-care-when-struggle (unit 4) | From planning care that costs to a support plan with checkpoints. |
| g8-soc-read-feelings (SO4) | 16 | g9-soc-read-feelings (unit 4) | From reading hidden cues in a group to planning a check-in and testing the reading. |
